Package: lunduke-linux-kernel
Version: 7.2.6-lcos17
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: 28
Maintainer: LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>
Homepage: https://lunduke.com
Depends: linux-image-7.2.6-lunduke (= 7.2.6-lcos17)
Recommends: linux-headers-7.2.6-lunduke (= 7.2.6-lcos17)
Description: Lunduke's Linux Kernel for LCOS
 Lunduke's Linux Kernel — LCOS kernel package (ABI lcos17).
 .
 Installs linux-image-7.2.6-lunduke. Headers are recommended for
 building out-of-tree modules.
 .
 lcos17 adds the SMB2/SMB3 network file system client on frozen
 lcos16: cifs (CONFIG_CIFS=m, CONFIG_CIFS_XATTR=y, LCOS#111), so
 Windows, Samba, and NAS shares mount with cifs-utils. SMB1 legacy
 dialects (CIFS_ALLOW_INSECURE_LEGACY), SMB Direct, and the ksmbd
 server stay off. Rust left off (No Forced Rust). No firmware blob is
 included. Proprietary NVIDIA is not included.
 .
 LCOS 0.8 ISOs shipped 7.2.6-lcos12; that config stays frozen.
 lcos13, lcos14, lcos15, and lcos16 stay frozen. This package is the
 lcos17 revision of the same linux-image-7.2.6-lunduke name. On earlier
 LCOS releases that still ship a Distro kernel, installing this
 metapackage adds a GRUB entry alongside it.
